{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, keep my words, and lay up my commandments with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Keep my commandments, and live; and my law as the apple of thy eye.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bind them upon thy fingers, write them upon the table of thy heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say to wisdom, Thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my sister; and call understanding ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " kinswoman:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may keep thee from the strange woman, from the stranger ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " flattereth with her words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For at the window of my house I looked through my casement,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And beheld among the simple ones, I discerned among the youths, a young man void of understanding,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Passing through the street near her corner; and he went the way to her house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the twilight, in the evening, in the black and dark night:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And behold, there met him a woman ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the attire of a harlot, and subtil of heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(She ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " loud and stubborn; her feet abide not in her house:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is she",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without, now in the streets, and lieth in wait at every corner.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So she caught him, and kissed him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with an impudent face said to him,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " peace-offerings with me; this day have I paid my vows.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I came forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have decked my bed with coverings of tapestry, with carved ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "works",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", with fine linen of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning: let us solace ourselves with loves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the good-man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not at home, he is gone a long journey:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath taken a bag of money with him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will come home at the day appointed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With her much fair speech she caused him to yield, with the flattering of her lips she impelled him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He goeth after her quickly, as an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as a fool to the correction of the stocks;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Till a dart striketh through his liver; as a bird hasteth to the snare, and knoweth not that it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for his life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now therefore hearken to me, O ye children, and attend to the words of my mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not thy heart decline to her ways, go not astray in her paths.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For she hath cast down many wounded: yes, many strong ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " have been slain by her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.7.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Her house ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the way to hell, going down to the chambers of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
